==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|twerc|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|twerc|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dwergaz}}. The development Middle High German ''tw-'' → modern German ''zw-'' is regular. Compare Dutch {{term|dwerg|lang=nl}}, English {{term|dwarf|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|dværg|lang=da}}.

